---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { pages } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout page={pages["design-support"]}>
  <section class="section intro">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO INTRODUCTION</p>
      <h2>
        A small canvas.
        <br />
        <em>A big part of your brand.</em>
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="lead">
        Already have artwork? Brilliant. Starting with a rough idea? You’re in the right
        place.
      </p>
      <p>
        Choose artwork supplied or design support when requesting a quote. We’ll help
        define a clear visual direction around your identity, your details and the way you
        want to connect.
      </p>
      <a class="button dark" href="/contact/?design=support">
        Tell us about your design ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section soft">
    <div class="three-grid">
      <article>
        <span class="step-num">01 / BRIEF</span>
        <h3>Start with your story.</h3>
        <p>
          Share your logo, brand colours, contact details, print route and a few
          references. Tell us whether you need NFC, a QR code, or both.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="step-num">02 / DIRECTION</span>
        <h3>Make room for the details.</h3>
        <p>
          We agree the design scope and cost in your quote. Legibility, hierarchy and
          sufficient space for an optional QR guide the layout.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="step-num">03 / APPROVAL</span>
        <h3>Check it. Then check it again.</h3>
        <p>
          Review the artwork and contact information before production. Check spelling,
          numbers, encoded data and your intended device compatibility.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section intro">
    <h2>
      Ready-made artwork?
      <br />
      <em>Let’s keep it sharp.</em>
    </h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        Send a vector logo where available, use high-quality images and keep essential
        information away from the edge. Request the final size, bleed and file
        specification before exporting.
      </p>
      <a class="inline-link" href="/articles/artwork-checklist/">
        Read the artwork checklist ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
